  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 250 AM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nThe long term period is shaping up to be fairly consistent \nthrough Friday. Starting Tuesday afternoon, we transition to \nmore of a southwest upper-level flow. This will usher in several\ndays of mostly sunny skies with high temperatures forecast in \nthe upper 60s to low 70s through Friday. The western county \nwarning area (CWA) could see some breezy afternoons with wind \ngusts around 25 mph possible. Compared to previous runs, models \nhave overall backed down on the wind potential for Tuesday \nafternoon, but NBM still has around a 30% chance for wind gusts \nover 30 mph for Kit Carson county. \n\nFriday, a trough off the coast of British Columbia will begin \nto dig south and has the potential to switch us to more of an \nactive weather pattern. Models are uncertain on the track and \nevolution of the deepening trough, but beginning Friday \nafternoon through Sunday evening, several embedded shortwave \npassages are forecast to move through the area bringing chances \nfor precipitation. Probability of Precipitation (PoPs) are \naround 20-30%, increasing from west to east. Precipitation \nchances and amounts will heavily depend on where the trough ends\nup setting up and how quickly it moves through the area. \nRegardless of precipitation chances, temperatures are forecast \nto be pleasant Friday through Sunday with highs in the 60s to \n70s across the region.",
